<title>NETHERLANDS: MeesPierson acts on fund irregularities.</title>
<headline>MeesPierson acts on fund irregularities.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch investment bank MeesPierson, wholly-owned by ABN AMRO NV, said on Tuesday it had discovered and addressed &quot;procedural irregularities&quot; within a U.S. investment fund, for which it acted as a sales agent.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the bank, which is being sold to Dutch/Belgian financial services group Fortis, declined to identify the fund and did not elaborate on the irregularities, found in an investigation.</p>
<p>&quot;There are no losses for the investors or the bank,&quot; spokesman Paul Fentrop told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
